The potential vulnerability is related to a Denial of Service (DoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises from the handling of zip file uploads without adequate validation of the file size or content. If the application allows excessively large zip files or files containing a large number of text files, it could lead to resource exhaustion on the server, such as high memory usage or CPU consumption, potentially causing the service to become unresponsive or crash. This lack of constraints on input size and complexity can be exploited by an attacker to disrupt the availability of the web application.

